{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And Elohim heard.</b> This teaches that she prayed to HaShem." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that He understood and knew her intention in the act — that it was for the purpose of a mitzvah, and out of her love for HaShem blessed be He and for His commandments. She disrupted the configuration [of supernal roots] through this act, and HaShem too disrupted the configuration, for according to the configuration she would have had only four sons ascend, but she conceived and bore a fifth son beyond the configuration, and a sixth — measure for measure."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:03.298694470Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}